<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dorudon atrox Turing wavelength at 253 µm, Priabonian 37.0 Ma (pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The PDE, Jacobian, onset formula, and equal-diffusion control match Turing's conditions and are asserted in self_test. Lean checks the integer margin, the equal-diffusion margin, and 3×253 = 759, 8×253 = 2024. Above onset the fastest mode (251.3 µm) is not identical to the onset wavenumber (253 µm); both are reported. The periodic nonlinear field becomes spots; the ocellus is the radial eigenmode, which the periodic square does not preserve." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0.py L199–L231: periodic square produces spots rather than a single radial ocellus <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L199-L231>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dorudon-atrox-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dorudon atrox Turing wavelength at 253 µm, Priabonian 37.0 Ma (pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
